  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $C$ to the line $\\overset{\u27f7}{AB},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\u27f7}{AB}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/ff359409206e3762233b6db6159b00b69d95124e8c1bd21597c36a9fde535f3f.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $C$ to $\\overset{\u27f7}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/71ec54229cf44e84d09a0ba315318a185ac83a235df109d17428581d21154a93.png)",
